# Zone 1, room 2 (grey box, Phase 1 task 7): tech 2, dash-jump.
# BUILD.md s5, tech 2: "carry dash speed into a jump. Taught by a gap exactly one dash-jump wide:
# since the air jump, the air dash and the Ember Toss carry every route further, that is a width
# only a route with a dash-jump crosses, 1664 u for Ash over a pit, 62 u past the farthest route
# without one (docs/adr/0010; tools/replay/gap_reach.gd measures it)"; s15 "Dash-jump ... clears the
# reference gap" (the checklist's "zone 1 room 7": it is this room, the second of the zone).
#
# Layout: the west hall, a safe first encounter (a ditch 6 tiles wide and 3 deep with a floor in it:
# a running jump crosses it, and a fall into it only costs a climb out), an island 15 tiles
# (480 u) long to run up on, then the chasm: 52 tiles (1664 u) over a pit 6 tiles below the
# ledges, its far face smooth (nothing to cling to or kick off), then the east ledge.
# The chasm is exactly tests/replay/rooms/chasm.room's, from the near edge (tile 33 here, 15 there)
# to the east ledge, 18 tiles to the right and 7 down; tests/unit/tools/test_gap_reach_room.gd
# holds the two equal, so gap_reach.gd's measurement of test/longchasm is this room's: 62 u more
# than the farthest route without a dash-jump (a ground dash-jump with its air jump alone clears it
# from dash frame 5 to 9 in a few ticks; the air dash makes it comfortable).
# Stand-ins: none (a pit is a pit).
room zone1/02_dash_jump
size 100 34
